{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  ucas: it(x: i8) = x^2\n  ucas: range it\nrange of it -> i8:\n  -127..121   (44 distinct values)\n  values: -127, -124, -119, -112..-111, -103, -95, -92, -87, -79, -71, -63, -60, -55, -47, -39, -31, -28, -23, -15, -7, 0..1, 4, 9, 16..17, ...\n  fits in i8\n  over all 256 points of the domain\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "what is the range of x squared for a signed byte x?", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["it(x: i8) = x^2", "range it"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "range", "type": "i8", "empty": false, "exhaustive": true, "points": 256, "undefined_points": 0, "min": {"value": -127, "exact": "-127"}, "max": {"value": 121, "exact": "121"}, "distinct": 44, "values": [-127, -124, -119, -112, -111, -103, -95, -92, -87, -79, -71, -63, -60, -55, -47, -39, -31, -28, -23, -15, -7, 0, 1, 4, 9, 16, 17, 25, 33, 36, 41, 49, 57, 64, 65, 68, 73, 81, 89, 97, 100, 105, 113, 121], "fits": "i8"}]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "exhaustive", "text": "every point of the domain evaluated"}, "files": [], "text": "  ucas: it(x: i8) = x^2\n  ucas: range it\nrange of it -> i8:\n  -127..121   (44 distinct values)\n  values: -127, -124, -119, -112..-111, -103, -95, -92, -87, -79, -71, -63, -60, -55, -47, -39, -31, -28, -23, -15, -7, 0..1, 4, 9, 16..17, ...\n  fits in i8\n  over all 256 points of the domain\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  ucas: it(x) = log(x)\n  ucas: show it\nit(x: real) = log(x)\n  -> real\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 2, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "what is log of x", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["it(x) = log(x)", "show it"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "show", "definition": "it(x: real) = log(x)", "body": "log(x)", "type": "real"}]}, "notes": [{"kind": "default", "text": "\"log\" without a base: the default, the natural log, ln (args.defaults)"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "  ucas: it(x) = log(x)\n  ucas: show it\nit(x: real) = log(x)\n  -> real\n"}, "isError": false}}
